    "Download and install without asking, applying it the next time Cmd-Tab starts. Off keeps the decision yours — this app owns ⌘-Tab for the whole machine, so replacing itself mid-session is worth a prompt.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Download and install without asking, applying it the next time Cmd-Tab starts. Off keeps the decision yours — this app owns ⌘-Tab for the whole machine, so replacing itself mid-session is worth a prompt."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Drag a window's title bar to a screen edge or corner to tile it there. Independent of the shortcuts below — you can have either, or both.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Drag a window's title bar to a screen edge or corner to tile it there. Independent of the shortcuts below — you can have either, or both."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Each opens the switcher on part of the window list instead of all of it. Held and released like the main trigger, and never sticky — a scoped cycle is a quick jump, not a panel to browse.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Each opens the switcher on part of the window list instead of all of it. Held and released like the main trigger, and never sticky — a scoped cycle is a quick jump, not a panel to browse."
